      text: "What are the severe weather events and climate extremes associated with El-Ni\u00f1o?",
      marks: 5,
      suggestedAnswer: "El-Ni\u00f1o: Anomalous warming of central and eastern tropical Pacific, occurring every 2\u20137 years, disrupting global atmospheric circulation.\n\nAssociated Climate Extremes:\n1. India \u2014 Deficient Monsoon: 22 of 29 major Indian droughts (1871\u20132018) occurred in El-Ni\u00f1o years; 2023 El-Ni\u00f1o caused below-normal monsoon.\n2. Australia \u2014 Droughts and Bushfires: Eastern Australia experiences drought; 2019-20 catastrophic bushfires coincided with El-Ni\u00f1o.\n3. Americas \u2014 Flooding: Heavy rainfall in coastal Peru and Ecuador; 1997-98 El-Ni\u00f1o caused $45 billion global damage.\n4. East Africa \u2014 Flooding: Unusual heavy rainfall in Kenya and Ethiopia.\n5. Global Temperature: El-Ni\u00f1o years are typically the warmest globally; 2023-24 was hottest on record partly due to El-Ni\u00f1o.\n6. Marine Impact: Coral bleaching in Pacific and Indian Oceans; collapse of Peruvian fisheries.\n\nIndia's Response: IMD monitors El-Ni\u00f1o/La-Ni\u00f1a conditions as a key input for seasonal monsoon forecasts."
