      id: "q4_d_2016",
      text: "Discuss the role of the Comptroller and Auditor General of India.",
      marks: 5,
      suggestedAnswer: "(See 2019 GS Q4(b) answer \u2014 CAG covered there comprehensively.)\n\nKey Summary:\n- Article 148: CAG \u2014 independent constitutional authority.\n- Functions: Audit of Union, State, and PSU accounts; certify government accounts; submit reports to President/Governor; examined by Public Accounts Committee.\n- Landmark reports: 2G, Coalgate, CWG \u2014 demonstrating constitutional watchdog role.\n- Significance: Parliament's 'eyes and ears' \u2014 essential for financial accountability."
